 and have them feel authentic but  the animators of wreck-it Ralph did just  that one of the original supervising  animators  five of the Disney Princesses was on  staff to help bring the princess crew  back Mark Ken was the genius behind  Ariel Belle jasmine Mulan and Tiana he  was there every step of the way to help  the newer younger animators make this  movie epic it's got to be great to work  with some of the biggest names in Disney  ever it must be a dream come true just  like vanilla peas dream for exciting  races Mario reference in the first  wreck-it Ralph we get to see a ton of  classic videogame characters like  pac-man and Sonic the Hedgehog and while  they reference Mario the iconic plumber  turned hero never makes an appearance he  didn't exactly make an appearance in the  sequel either but there was a very  subtle reference you might have missed  when Ralph and vanellope first look out  over the World Wide Web there is a  hologram toadstool shooting out of  Rainbow Road classic Mario fans will  totally get this reference  maybe one day Mario will get a Disney  cameo until then we'll just keep looking  for Easter eggs drawing frenzy Ralph  breaks the Internet is one ambitious  film it attempts to make social  commentary on internet culture through  tons of jokes it succeeds it has  messages about friendship and so many  pop-culture references we couldn't keep  track a movie this huge had a lot of  work to go into it did you know that  there were 280 3839 drawings that went  into this sequel how insane is that most  of them did get thrown out but what made  it into the movie is amazing working on  a movie like Ralph breaks the Internet  must have been so much fun  post-credit scenes if you watched all  the trailers for a Ralph's breaks the  internet you were probably pretty  excited to see Ralph overstep a bunny in  an online game but that scene didn't  make it into the main part of the movie  we hate it when that happens but so does  Disney they included this scene in the  first post-credit scene and they threw  in a joke about how disappointing it is  when a scene from a trailer isn't in the  film we love that they can laugh at  themselves how about that second  post-credit scene we don't want to spoil  it for you but it was not what we  expected at all did you stay to watch  the extra  scenes they were so worth it keep  watching for our favorite secret from  the new movie so many Easter eggs it's  impossible to know how many Easter eggs  and pop-culture references are in  Ralph's breaks the Internet there are so  many that even if filmmakers aren't sure  how many there are according to Larry Wu  the head of environments they had  several meetings to comb the film and  make lists of all of them but they know  they missed some because different  animators sneaked in little secrets  where should you look for the most  Easter eggs watch the eBay scene and oh  my Disney scene carefully and see how  many you can find some you would never  guess like animators names Loftus  Steiner one of the most subtle secrets  is found in the billboard at the very  beginning and very end of the movie we  are shown outside of the arcade behind  it is a billboard for Loftus Steiner  that seems like a weird random name for  a breakfast place don't you think how  did the animators come up with that the  answer is in the credits  Cory Loftus is the production designer  for a route breaks the Internet he's so  important that he gets his very first  and very last Easter egg in the movie if  those sneaky animators do you think  Loftus put it in the movie himself or  was someone trying to impress their boss  owed to Wikipedia the amount of Internet  jokes and references in Ralph's breaks  the Internet is insane  there are birds that tweet on Twitter  IMDB and Fandango show up Google is  nearly taken down by wreck-it ralph  virus and the giant pin from Pinterest  is used as a weapon we see all our  favorite websites and apps mentioned and  no internet movie would be complete  without a reference to wikipedia the  free encyclopedia is obviously very  important to the animators toward the  end of the movie when Ralph and  vanellope are trying to stop the virus  we see a huge statue honoring Wikipedia  it's literally put on a pedestal we know  we know Wikipedia is great but we aren't  sure we dedicate a statue to it would  you the gang's all here most of our  favorite characters from wreck-it Ralph  we're back fix-it Felix and Captain  Calhoun are happily married tapper and  sour bill are still around mr. Litvak is  still voiced by Ed O'Neill even taffeta  voiced by Mindy Kaling returned for the  sequel but the crazy villain from the  first movie King candy aka turbo met his  demise but his voice actor returned as a  new character Alan Tudyk played no  more the searchbar guy we're so happy  that he got to come back in their new  movie I'm sorry but my autofill is a  touch aggressive today what was your  favorite part of brows breaks the  internet let us know in the comments  below and that's it for the 10 secrets  from Ralph breaks the internet check out  our community page for more great  content and don't forget to subscribe  see you next time  [Music]

